# Operate — native subagent delegation

When running `/operate`, `operate-agent-system`, or implementing work from an
`agent-system/` prompt pack:

1. Parent chat = Principal Architect / orchestrator only.
2. For each selected specialist (any agent other than the orchestrator), use
   Cursor **Task** when available.
3. Each Task prompt must include that agent’s `agent-system/agents/*.md`
   purpose and the filled `task-delegation.yaml` for this request.
4. Do not role-play `backend-engineer`, `frontend-engineer`, `qa-engineer`,
   or other fleet specialists in the parent turn while Task is available.
5. After Task returns, integrate the handoff in the parent and continue the
   operate loop (next agent, QA Task, or integration review).

When running `/operate`, also use **`AskQuestion`** for A–E menus when available.

Full procedure: `core/workflows/operate-agent-system.md` (§ Delegation runtime).
Cursor tool names: `.cursor/skills/operate-agent-system/SKILL.md`.
